  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Philippines: Sustainable Training and Education in the Philippines for Justice Professionals (STEP4JP)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">1) To ensure that the Supreme Court, the Department of Justice, the Office of the Ombudsman and the Anti-Money Laundering Council (&#x2018;target institutions&#x2019;) have advanced trainers who can conduct training of trainers. 2) To increase the number of justice sector trainers in the target institutions. 3) To ensure that targeted justice sector trainers have the ability to conduct training on legal subject matters. 4) To ensure that the capacity development agencies in the target institutions have a high-quality strategic plan. 5) To ensure that the policies of the target institutions foster and retain high-quality trainers. 6) To ensure that the target institutions have systems to manage the learning needs of their professional staff. 7) To ensure that the target institutions and their international development partners have venues where they can exchange ideas and compare strategies on capacity development. 8) To ensure that the target institutions stage interagency learning events.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Direct beneficiaries: Anti-Money Laundering Council (AMLC), Department of Justice (DOJ), Office of the Ombudsman (OMB), Supreme Court (SC). Indirect beneficiaries: Justice seekers and the wider population of the Philippines.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to develop the professional capacity of Philippine justice sector institutions to continuously improve the knowledge and skills of their staff and thereby improve the quality of justice delivery for the public.</narrative>
  </description>
